10. Interview Question

Q: When should we use WebSockets?

Answer:

WebSockets are used when we need real-time bidirectional communication between client and server.
Examples include chat applications, live notifications, stock market updates, and multiplayer games.
Unlike HTTP, WebSocket maintains a persistent connection allowing the server to push updates instantly without repeated client requests.